Notes on this run (added by hand, 2026-11-08):
- Step 9 failed only because the script read proposal #2 one block too early: the RPC node had not caught up with
  the block that created it, so get_proposal returned nothing. Step 11 then read the same proposal fine: still
  InProgress, unpaid. The script now waits until a proposal is readable, and /api/vote waits for the voter's own vote
  before updating the Telegram card (lib/pot.ts waitForVote).
- The bot refusing to vote was also exercised on testnet during development: on cm-mw75i7gq.sputnikv2.testnet the
  bot's act_proposal and a ChangePolicy proposal both failed with ERR_PERMISSION_DENIED, and 2 of 2 council votes
  paid out (tx 2GqwhpUEwZ2WPMRqtqv99JsiYoZZcDKpmHdWk17RUFrH).
- A fresh full run was not possible right after the fix: the testnet faucet allows only a few accounts per IP per day
  and the sponsor had 1.96 NEAR left, less than the 6 NEAR a new DAO locks for storage.

